    {
        "content": "<p>xia-chao edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988\">PR #14988</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>two host headers currently get one of them picked as the authority and handed to the guest. #14915 fixed the same kind of guessing for scheme, so this rejects the request with a 400 per rfc 9112 3.2 instead.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 634771091,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792945582
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"repeat\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f501\" role=\"img\" title=\"repeat\">:repeat:</span> pchickey submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14988#pullrequestreview-5657726982\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So, the RFC gives a couple of conditions here and we are detecting them piecemeal. To me, this means its time to create a single helper function <code>get_request_target(&amp;Request) -&gt; Result&lt;Authority&gt;</code>, which has rustdocs saying it enforces the full set of conditions in <a href=\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9112/#section-3.2\">https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9112/#section-3.2</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A server MUST respond with a 400 (Bad Request) status code to any HTTP/1.1 request message that lacks a Host header field and to any request message that contains more than one Host header field line or a Host header field with an invalid field value.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>And some of that can be de-duplicated out of the p3 branch of code into that auxillary function. In the p2 branch it can just <code>let _ = authority;</code> so it builds without warnings when p3 disabled.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635133231,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793042443
    },
